\par\par \b \uc2 China's Yuan Falls to Seven-Month Low -3-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anjani Trivedi   \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2015\par 09:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 China's yuan fell sharply Monday to its weakest level in seven months, pushed lower by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Beijing adds to a host of measures aimed at spurring growth.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the morning reference rate--which typically sets the daily direction--weaker, with traders then pushing the yuan down to the closest it has ever been to the weak side of its 2% daily trading band. The band was widened in March last year.\par \par \uc2 China's move comes as many other large economies seek to boost growth with weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week announced larger-than-expected stimulus measures, which sent the euro tumbling to its lowest levels in over 11 years, while emerging-market giant India has also surprised markets with an interest-rate cut this month. The U.S. recovery continues to remain on track.\par \par \uc2 For China, a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should help two key elements of the world's second-biggest economy: exports and inflation. Data last week showed China was growing at its slowest pace in almost 25 years, while inflation has fallen to a five-year low, sparking worries over building deflationary pressures and spluttering growth. A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes it more expensive to import goods from rest of the world, which spurs inflation.\par \par \uc2 The country has recently made a range of stealth measures, including slashing interest rates for the first time in over two years in November and last week allowing banks additional room to lend--but has so far avoided announcing outright monetary easing policy measures.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say however that the moves to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few days has been the opposite of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's guidance in December, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fixed at a stronger level but traders still pushed the yuan weaker.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases data for December 2014 released last week showed that the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  had sold $23.1 billion, the largest net amount sold since January 2000, according to analysts from ANZ, pointing to signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be selling dollars and buying the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December indicates that the [\uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] may be uncomfortable with the pace of yuan depreciation, and sought to cap the upward move" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, Khoon Goh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at the ANZ, wrote in a note to clients Monday. A higher number for the yuan against the U.S. dollar means a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yuan ended 2014 down 2.4% against the U.S. dollar, its largest annual loss and first drop since 2009. This year so far, it is down 0.9%.\par \par \uc2 Other investors and analysts say that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements are part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to make the unit more market-driven.\par \par \uc2 "This is still part of the volatility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to see, instead of a directional trend shift, compared with the past," said Kewei Yang, head of interest rates strategy in Asia Pacific at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Yang said that policy makers have to be careful when guiding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker, especially in an environment where the U.S. dollar is strengthening, which could add further downward pressure on the yuan.\par \par \uc2 The yuan last traded at 6.2537 against the U.S. dollar, and was fixed at 6.1384.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anjani Trivedi at anjani.trivedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 26-01-15 0845GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150126eb1q00080\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
