\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises despite a slightly lower midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2015\par 04:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Jan 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose against the\par dollar on Wednesday though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official\par midpoint a shade lower than the previous day.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the midpoint at\par 6.1269 per dollar, slightly down from Tuesday's 6.1256.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.2079 near midday, up 0.08\par percent from Tuesday's close at 6.2130. It traded at a narrow\par range between 6.2063 and 6.2141 in morning trade.\par     "Demand to sell dollars is still strong today," said a\par trader at a Chinese bank in Shanghai, adding that the bid and\par ask price gap was wide due to cautious market sentiment.\par     A slowing down economy is fueling expectations of more\par policy easing measures this year, which in turn will keep\par downward pressure on the yuan.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  expected China's GDP growth to slow further to 6.8\par percent in 2015 and rising deflationary pressure to spur the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut benchmark lending rates by at least 50 basis\par points this year.\par     "We expect the RMB to depreciate modestly against the USD\par (6.35 by end 2015) amid a likely volatile EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par environment," its economist Wang Tao said.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.    \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:         \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1269     6.1256       -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.2079     6.213        0.08%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.32%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.48%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 33.32%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:            \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2115    0.01%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.3115    -2.92%\par  forwards               **                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michelle Chen\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; Editing by Gopakumar Warrier)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-7T04:45:27.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150107eb17002pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
