\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips on weaker midpoint, dollar strength\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2015\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Jan 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged down against\par the dollar on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the weakest\par official midpoint in nearly a month to reflect strength in the\par global dollar index.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the midpoint at\par 6.1248 per dollar, down 0.09 percent from the previous trading\par day on Dec. 31. It was the weakest level since Dec. 8.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.2204 near midday,\par down 0.26 percent from last Wednesday's close at 6.2040. The\par Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost 2.4 percent in 2014, its first significant\par annual loss since its landmark revaluation in 2005.\par     Further policy easing by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  to help prop up slowing\par growth will likely keep downward pressure on the yuan this year,\par traders said. But a Reuters poll in December estimates that the\par yuan will rebound to 6.05 per dollar in a year's time despite\par policy easing. \par     China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was closed Jan. 1-2 for the\par New Year holiday and resumed trading on Jan. 5. \par     The dollar index, which measures the greenback\par against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , hit a fresh nearly\par nine-year high of 91.131 on Friday and notched its third\par straight weekly gain. \par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.    \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                         Current    Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint                6.1248     6.119      -0.09%\par  Spot yuan                    6.2204     6.204      -0.26%\par  Divergence from midpoint*    1.56%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.68%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 33.05%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2292    -0.04%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.3345    -3.31%\par  forwards               **                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michelle Chen\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacqueline Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-5T05:00:49.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150105eb1500393\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
