\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan set for first big loss since 2005\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2014\par 05:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 31 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged up against\par the dollar on Wednesday following a stronger midpoint set by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but looked set to post its first significant\par yearly loss since its landmark revaluation in 2005.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the official\par midpoint at 6.1190 per dollar, 0.06 percent higher than\par Tuesday's 6.1224. \par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1990 near midday, up\par 0.05 percent from the pervious day's close at 6.2020. It briefly\par touched 6.1908 in morning trade, the highest level since Dec 25.\par   \par     Traders said the new rules on the management of banks'\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  net opening positions (NOP) released by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Administration of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (SAFE) on Tuesday\par supported the yuan.\par     China will relax restrictions on banks' yuan trading from\par Jan 1, replacing daily caps on banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positions\par with weekly limits, leaving them leeway to short dollars within\par that period. \par     "The fact that some banks will be exempted from being forced\par to keep minimum long dollar position may alleviate pressure on\par RMB depreciation. As such, we think the upside for USD/CNY will\par be capped in the near term," said Xie Dongming, an economist at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.    \par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell sharply early this year in what\par was widely seen as an engineered move by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par crack down on speculators betting on one-way appreciation.\par     It regained some ground later in the year, but tumbled again\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets but cutting the\par benchmark interest rate in November to shore up the slowing\par economy. Further policy easing is expected in coming months,\par which will keep downward pressure on the yuan.\par     A series of weak economic indicators have added to the\par bearish sentiment toward the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Activity in China's\par factory sector shrank for the first time in seven months in\par December, a private survey showed on Wednesday.\par     The final \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 /Markit Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for\par December came in at 49.6, just below the 50.0 level that\par separates growth from contraction.        \par     The yuan is poised to end the year down 2.4 percent, its\par first meaningful annual depreciation since 2005. It had dipped\par fractionally in 2009.\par     By comparison, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained 2.8 percent in 2013.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint. It traded 1.3 percent lower than the\par midpoint in morning trade.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.119      6.1224       0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.199      6.202        0.05%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.31%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.34%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 33.51%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current    Difference\par                                            from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2146     0.05%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.345      -3.56%\par  forwards               **                 \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michelle Chen\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-31T05:31:17.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141231eacv0050m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
