\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips after c.bank again sets weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2014\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged down\par against the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the\par lowest midpoint in two weeks.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the official\par midpoint at 6.1230 per dollar, down 0.02 percent from Monday's\par 6.1220. It was the lowest level since Dec. 9 and the fourth\par consecutive weaker midpoint.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.2257 near midday,\par down 0.07 percent from the previous day's close at 6.2216. \par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under depreciation pressure\par since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Nov. 21 surprisingly cut benchmark\par interest rates. \par     Last week was the fourth straight one in which the yuan\par declined against the dollar.    \par     Investor bets on the yuan turned bearish for the first time\par since June, according to a Reuters poll on Dec. 18, which showed\par investor sentiment toward most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par remained bearish. \par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.123      6.122        -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.2257     6.2216       -0.07%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.68%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.76%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 32.94%\par  \par     *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative\par number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the\par midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange\par rate to rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it\par sets each morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current    Difference from\par                                            onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2235     -0.08%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.358      -3.70%\par  forwards               **                 \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}