\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips vs dlr after another weaker midpoint fixed\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2014\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan slipped on\par Monday, putting it in line with the degree to which other\par emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have weakened, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed\par the daily midpoint weaker against the dollar for a third\par straight day.    \par     In early trade on Monday, the yuan weakened to 6.2240 per\par dollar compared to 6.2202 on Friday. Last week was the fourth in\par a row in which the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declined against the dollar.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed the daily midpoint at 6.1220 per\par dollar on Monday compared to 6.1205 per dollar on Friday.    \par     Chinese traders turned sharply bearish on the yuan in late\par November, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made a surprise cut to interest\par rates, seen as a sign of easing to come and by extension\par downward pressure on the yuan's relative value. \par     Traders turned sharply bearish on the yuan in late November,\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprisingly cut interest rates. That was\par taken as a sign there will be more easing, which in turn\par extended downward pressure on the yuan. \par     Another factor contributing to the weakness in the yuan are\par steadily declining purchases of dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market by \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial institutions,\par indicating pressure on the renminbi to appreciate has eased\par considerably. \par     On Sunday, state radio quoted the deputy chief of \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as saying the yuan will stay basically stable\par despite fluctuations.              \par  \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:  \par  Item                        Current     Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.122       6.1205      -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                   6.224       6.2202      -0.06%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   1.67%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                     -2.73%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  32.98%\par  \par     *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative\par number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the\par midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange\par rate to rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it\par sets each morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET  \par     Weekly CNH Tracker in PDF: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tuv63w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tuv63w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par          \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:       \par  Instrument                      Current     Difference from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.2241      0.02%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.359       -3.73%\par  forwards               **                   \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>