\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan set for third biggest weekly fall in 2014\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2014\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 19 (Reuters) - China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is on track\par for its third biggest weekly loss against the dollar this year\par as a resurgent greenback finally caught up with the renminbi in\par the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  complex.\par     A 12 percent rise in the dollar index - which tracks\par the greenback against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- neared\par a five-year peak on Friday leaving other emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from India to Indonesia reeling. \par     But the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has mostly held its own against the\par dollar thanks to a rally in the onshore stock markets and a\par broadly appreciating bias evident from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par fixings.\par     That support gave way this week after data showed activity\par in China's factory sector contracted in December for the first\par time in seven months prompting some investors to yank some\par bullish yuan bets off the table. \par     In early trades on Friday, the yuan fell quickly past a key\par technical level of 6.2271 -- the 76.4 percent retracement of the\par May to October range -- despite tepid moves in the broad dollar\par index. The yuan closed at 6.2163 per dollar on Thursday.\par     "Some key technical levels on dollar/yuan are being broken\par on the topside and this is largely due to year-end positioning\par flows and after the recent rising streak in the last few\par months," said Dominic Bunning, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Hong Kong.\par    The weakness in the economy has led to calls for more\par government stimulus measures and a cut in banks' reserve\par requirements after a surprise interest rate cut last month\par raising concerns the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may remain weak in the near term.\par     Despite the 0.6 percent fall against the dollar so far this\par week, market conditions remain orderly with the gap between the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in the offshore and the onshore market remaining\par below levels seen earlier this year.\par     On Friday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed the daily midpoint at\par 6.1205 per dollar compared with 6.1195 on Thursday.\par     In the derivative markets, both non-deliverable and\par deliverable offshore forward rates in the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reflected the weakness in the spot rate and edged higher.    \par  \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:       \par  Item                        Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1205     6.1195      -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                   6.2238     6.2163      -0.12%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   1.69%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.73%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 32.98%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET  \par     Weekly CNH Tracker in PDF: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tuv63w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tuv63w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par          \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:       \par  Instrument                      Current     Difference from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.2248      -0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.353       -3.66%\par  forwards               **                   \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacqueline Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-19T04:13:51.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141219eacj003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
