\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan at 5-month lows after weak fixing\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan slumped to a\par five-month low against the dollar on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker daily midpoint fix, prompting investors to cut\par exposure to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     While emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been under pressure in\par recent days thanks to a rapid drop in oil prices and a financial\par crisis in Russia, China's yuan has been broadly steady as Bejing\par has steadfastly maintained a stronger fixing trend.\par     That series of strong fixings was broken conclusively on\par Thursday as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the official\par midpoint at 6.1195 per dollar, sharply weaker than Wednesday's\par 6.1137.\par     The weak fixing sparked a selloff as investors bet the yuan\par is likely to remain under pressure in the coming days in\par sympathy with the broader emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  complex.\par     Recent volatility in the mainland markets along with a rise\par in broad risk aversion, search for safety and falling market\par liquidity towards the year-end have exacerbated market moves.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists said in a note to clients that they see a\par risk of further emerging market weakness.\par     In a sign that Beijing remains confident about yuan's \par outlook, China's regulators said it will push forward with\par reforms to allow for full capital account convertibility.\par  \par     On Thursday, spot yuan weakened quickly to 6.2187\par per dollar, 0.34 percent weaker than Wednesday's close of 6.1975\par and comfortably settling above the 23.6 percent retracement line\par of the 2014 year high to low trading range.\par  \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:       \par  Item                        Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1195     6.1137      -0.09%\par  Spot yuan                   6.2153     6.1975      -0.29%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   1.57%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.60%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 33.16%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:       \par  Instrument                      Current     Difference from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.2179      -0.23%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.3395      -3.47%\par  forwards               **                   \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-18T04:57:35.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141218eaci002sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
