\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  guidance, weak flash PMI\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 16 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell against the\par dollar on Tuesday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker midpoint, and\par on further indications that China will roll out more stimulus\par measures to shore up the sluggish economy.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the official\par midpoint at 6.1182 per dollar, down 0.05 percent from the\par previous day's 6.1152.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1943 near midday,\par down 0.05 percent from Monday's close at 6.1912.\par     "There have been many explanations for the recent spike in\par USD/RMB, but we think the two most probable reasons are onshore\par corporate USD demand from oilers and/or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging of USD\par liabilities," Nomura analysts said in a note to clients.\par     But there was no sign of a shift in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to maintain the appreciation bias on\par the CNY fix into 2015, the Nomura analysts added. \par     The yuan has been under pressure in the past month as  \par demand for dollars from oil and coal companies increases near\par year-end, while a series of weak economic data from China\par implies more monetary easing ahead.\par     Activity in China's factory sector shrank in December for\par the first time in seven months as new orders declined, a\par preliminary private survey showed on Tuesday. \par     The flash \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 /Markit manufacturing purchasing managers'\par index (PMI) fell to a contractionary 49.5 in December from\par November's final reading of 50.0 and below the 50.0 reading\par forecast by the market.\par  \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:   \par  Item                        Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1182     6.1152      -0.05%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1943     6.1912      -0.05%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   1.24%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -2.27%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 33.61%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                      Current  Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1990   0.00%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.312    -3.07%\par  forwards               **                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michelle Chen\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; Editing by Eric Meijer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-16T04:59:56.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141216eacg003kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
