\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan firms after sharp slide as traders suspect c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2014\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * C.bank suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after record yuan slip\par     * Official fixing rate strongest since March\par     * Spot rate up 0.12 percent at midday\par     * Yuan continues to trade below midpoint\par \par     By Jake Spring\par     BEIJING, Dec 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened\par against the dollar on Wednesday, recovering from a sharp slide\par in the previous session, with some traders suspecting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is propping up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behind closed doors in\par the name of maintaining stability.\par     The spot yuan lost more than 0.5 percent against\par the dollar in intraday trade on Tuesday, in what would have been\par its sharpest daily decline since 2008, as corporates bailed out\par of yuan in the face of disappointing trade indicators and\par rumours of monetary easing, seen as diluting the yuan's relative\par value.\par     The sharpness of the slide tested the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's (\f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) public commitment to reduce \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the name of broader financial reform, which\par it backed up with a liberalisation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's trading\par band, widened to 2 percent on either side of the midpoint this\par year. \par     However, while easing is supposed to be bearish for the\par yuan, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been bullish with its guidance rate\par , pushing it to firm by 0.35 percent since Dec 4,\par considered a signal to the market to maintain rate stability.\par     However, markets shrugged off that guidance on Monday and\par Tuesday, and some traders believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  blinked on Wednesday,\par and instructed intermediaries to buy up yuan to head off a herd\par movement out of renminbi.\par     "As the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is suspected of having come into the market to\par support the yuan, the yuan is likely to stabilize around 6.2 to\par the dollar in the near term," said one trader at a Chinese bank\par in Shanghai.\par     The spot market opened down slightly from the previous close\par before rebounding to change hands at 6.178, up 0.12 percent.\par     Whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  did indeed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behind the scenes is\par difficult to discern. Another trader at a Chinese bank in\par Shanghai said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and would not enter\par the market unless there was a larger, more sustained movement in\par the yuan.\par     In spite of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts to support the yuan,\par the spot rate was 0.96 percent below the midpoint at midday.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has consistently traded below the midpoint\par since last week.\par     Following on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's surprise interest rate cut\par last month, it is predicted to cut the reserve requirement\par ratio, which would flood the market with yuan and dilute its\par value.\par     Lower consumer inflation figures released on Wednesday could\par further pave the way for an RRR cut, ANZ economists wrote in a\par note. Consumer inflation fell to 1.4 percent in November, down\par from 1.6 percent and missing expectations. \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item               Current   Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.1195    6.1231      0.06%\par                                         \par  Spot yuan          6.178     6.1855      0.12%\par                                         \par  Divergence from    0.96%               \par  midpoint*                              \par  Spot change ytd                        -2.01%\par  Spot change since 2005                 33.97%\par  revaluation                            \par  \par * Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     The prospect of a sliding onshore yuan is negative for the\par prospects of the offshore market, which has already seen\par outflows, thanks to the luanch of a landmark stock connect\par scheme that has drawn yuan flows out of Hong Kong into China.\par     By early December there was a net outflow of 44.7 billion\par yuan from Hong Kong's yuan pool since Nov. 17, as Shanghai-bound\par investment totalled 49.3 billion yuan while inflows into Hong\par Kong were a mere 4.6 billion yuan.                \par     \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument            Current  Difference\par                                 from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.1850     -0.11%\par           *                     \par  Offshore              6.312    -3.05%\par  non-deliverable                \par  forwards                       \par                **               \par  \par \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Additional reporting by Lu Jianxin in SHANGHAI and Michelle\par Chen in HONG KONG; Editing by Pete Sweeney)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-10T07:05:52.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141210eaca008yb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
