\par\par \b \uc2 China Yuan Falls to 4-Month Low on Weak Trade Data -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2014\par 10:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   Vs Parity  Previous \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.1282               6.1373 \par USD/CNY OTC 0830 GMT     6.1727    +0.73%     6.1502 \par             High         6.1727    +0.73% \par             Low          6.1478    +0.32% \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI--China's yuan fell to a four-month low against the U.S. dollar Monday on the back of weak Chinese economic data and after the dollar reached multiyear highs against the euro and yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The yuan was at 6.1727 to a dollar at the close--its weakest level since Aug. 5, when it touched 6.1782--compared with 6.1502 at Friday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded between 6.1478 and 6.1727 in the session.\par \par \uc2 China's exports rose 4.7% in November from a year earlier, down from an 11.6% rise in October and below forecast 8% growth. Imports fell 6.7% from a year earlier, after a 4.6% rise in October, missing the forecast 3.9% increase.\par \par \uc2 "The yuan has been falling since November and the latest data supported more weakness in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader, adding the yuan's downside limit will be decided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that traders didn't see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.1282, lower than Friday's 6.1373, despite the dollar's strength after data showed much stronger-than-expected U.S. job gains in November.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has fallen 1.9% since the start of 2014, with most of the losses in the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts rose to 6.3005/6.3045 from 6.2760/6.2810 late Friday, implying a 2% fall by the yuan over the next year.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at CNY6.1772, higher than CNY6.1534 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Wynne Wang at wynne.wang@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 08-12-14 0952GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020141208eac8000b4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
