\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slightly weaker, follows last week's bearish trend\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2014\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BEIJING, Dec 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened against the\par broadly stronger dollar on Monday, despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par setting a stronger official guidance rate.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the yuan's midpoint rate at\par 6.1282 per dollar prior to market open, 0.15 percent stronger\par than the previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to\par trade 2 percent above or below the midpoint.\par     Last week was the first time since August that the yuan\par consistently traded below the midpoint, indicating the challenge\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  faces keeping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable as many neighbors\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaken against the dollar.\par     The trend continued on Monday with a spot rate that was 0.44\par percent weaker than the midpoint.\par     Yuan changed hands at the spot rate of 6.1549 at midday,\par down 0.08 percent.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has resisted the temptation to guide the yuan lower\par to help boost soft exports and prop up the slowing economy. \par     China's November exports missed expectations on Monday\par , and GDP growth is expected to slip to a 24-year\par low of 7.4 percent this year.\par     In spite of this weak growth, China posted a record trade\par surplus of $54.5 billion for November. \par     Analysts said the size of the surplus may increase pressure\par to strengthen the yuan. Critics, particularly in the United\par States, often cite large trade surpluses as a sign the yuan is\par undervalued.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.1282   6.1373      0.15%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.1549   6.1502      -0.08%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.44%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -1.64%\par  Spot change since 2005                34.47%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument            Current  Difference\par                                 from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.1590   -0.07%\par           *                     \par  Offshore              6.2875   -2.53%\par  non-deliverable                \par  forwards                       \par                **               \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \h