\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan touches 3-1/2 month low on \uc2 PBOC\uc2  guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2014\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan touched a 3-1/2\par month low against the dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set weaker\par midpoint, but had steadied slightly from the low by midday on\par Thursday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the official\par midpoint at 6.1411 per dollar, down 0.06 percent from\par Wednesday's 6.1376. It was the lowest level since Nov 25.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1508 at midday, down\par 0.01 percent from the previous day's close at 6.1500. It touched\par 6.1599 in morning trade, the weakest level since Aug. 22.    \par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.      \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:        \par  Item                       Current      Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1411       6.1376      -0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1508       6.15        -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.16%                    \par  Spot change ytd                                     -1.58%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.56%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:          \par  Instrument                      Current      Difference fr