\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls to two-month lows, outlook remains cautious\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2014\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 3 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell to two-month\par lows against the dollar on Wednesday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened the midpoint to the lowest level since Nov 26.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixed the official midpoint at\par 6.1376 per dollar, down 0.08 percent from the previous day's\par 6.1325.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1512 near midday,\par down 0.01 percent from Tuesday's close at 6.1503. It briefly\par touched a two-month low of 6.1531 in morning trade. \par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.  \par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is under pressure with the economy\par losing momentum. It may take more stimulus than last month's\par interest rate cut to support rapid growth.\par      Some analysts expect the country's annual growth rate this\par year to fall below 7.5 percent, the slowest expansion in 24\par years.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:      \par  Item                         Current     Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint                6.1376      6.1325     -0.08%\par  Spot yuan                    6.1512      6.1503     -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*    0.22%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                     -1.58%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.55%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:      \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1532    0.07%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.264     -2.02%\par  forwards               **                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \