\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls to two-month lows as c.bank sets weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2014\par 03:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Dec 1 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell to two-month\par lows against the dollar on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set\par another weaker midpoint to reflect strength in the global dollar\par index.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixed the official midpoint at\par 6.1369 per dollar, down 0.04 percent from Friday's 6.1345.\par     The spot yuan changed hands at 6.1465 near\par midday, down 0.02 percent from Friday's close at 6.1450. It\par briefly touched 6.15 in morning trade, the lowest level since\par Sept 30.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     The yuan traded weaker than the official guidance rate last\par Tuesday for the first time since late September, as appetite for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wanes after a surprise rate cut last month.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current     Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1369      6.1345      -0.04%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1465      6.145       -0.02%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.16%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.51%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 34.65%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current  Difference from\par                                          onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1596   0.03%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.261    -1.98%\par  forwards               **               \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTE