\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Weakness Lies Ahead, Charts Suggest -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2014\par 04:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0336 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yuan has fallen as much as 0.6% since the start of November but this may just be the start of further weakness for China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The daily chart for spot USD/CNY is turning bullish, suggesting that the U.S. dollar has more room to rise. The dollar has been climbing since it entered the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--which now supports at 6.1357--on Monday and is now peeking out from the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. A Friday close above the 6.1438 top of the Cloud would enhance the bullish technical bias for spot USD/CNY. Confirmation of this chart signal would suggest USD/CNY is on its way to the 6.1676 entrance of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel. USD/CNY is now 6.1468 from its Thursday close of 6.1392. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0335 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India will be the biggest beneficiary of inaction from the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (\uc2 OPEC\uc2 ) as its import costs tumble, says Rahul Chadha, co-chief investment officer for \uc2 Mirae Asset Global Investments\uc2 , which manages $62bn in assets. \uc2 OPEC\uc2 's laissez-faire approach shouldn't have surprised anyone, he says: "For the last couple of months, statements coming from Saudi Arabia show that they're just not interested in cuts," he says. "For the last six to nine months we've been saying the big bull market in commodities is over. The biggest beneficiary of that is India." A reformist government and expectations of a rate cut from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  next year will also help, he adds. While Chadha says his fund hasn't changed allocations surrounding the \uc2 OPEC\uc2  meeting, it has gone overweight India "big time," increasing its weighting to 25%. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0333 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The lowest accepted price for today's 2-year JGB auction is likely around 100.18, traders say. The result of the Y2.7 trillion tender will be released at 0345 GMT. The latest issue carries a coupon of 0.1%, unchanged from the previous issue. That compares with a yield on already issued two-year JGBs that fell into negative territory for the first time ever this morning, hitting -0.005%, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's aggressive purchasing of JGBs continues to keep market conditions tight. Active buying by foreign investors is also seen as another factor driving the 2-year bond yield below zero, traders say. Lead December futures are unchanged at 146.88. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0331 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD is higher, tracking the rising USD/JPY and USD/KRW, says a local trader. The trader notes USD buying comes from both local and foreign investors. "In addition to demand from importers, we also saw USD remittance by local insurers," he says. But the TWD's declines are relatively smaller than the falls in the JPY and KRW as rising local stocks still provide the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with some support. The pair is at 30.929, higher than 30.870 traded before the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, which lifted it to 30.951 at the close of onshore trading session, traders say. The Taiex is 0.2% higher; foreign investors have been net buyers of local stocks for eight straight sessions. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India will be the biggest beneficiary of inaction from the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (\f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0329 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The NZD/USD is little changed as "markets are not interested in taking it anywhere ahead of next week" when a number of important global economic events are due, including U.S. nonfarm payrolls data, in addition to the GlobalDairyTrade auction, says ANZ senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager Sam Tuck. The pair is at 0.7849. Mr. Tuck says even though New Zealand business confidence was strong, it had little impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the pair remaining "smack bang" in its current trading range of 0.7700 to 0.8000. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] New Zealand third-quarter terms of trade are expected to fall from the quarter before and year-earlier as export prices are expected to be significantly lower, according to a Wall Street Journal poll of eight economists. The poll expects terms of trade to fall 4.8% from the quarter before and 0.3% from a year earlier. A fall in New Zealand's quarterly terms of trade would mean less imported goods could be funded by the country's exports in the third quarter versus the second. The median sees exports prices down 5.3% from the previous quarter, while import prices fell 0.1%. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  lowers the rating on Chinese property developer Renhe Commercial (1387.HK) to CC from CCC. The outlook is negative. "We downgraded Renhe because we view the company's recent tender offer on its senior unsecured notes as constituting a distressed exchange tantamount to an immediate default," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  credit analyst Christopher Yip. Renhe has offered to buy back outstanding US$900 million of notes at a discount of 7%-18% to their par value, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Renhe converts bomb shelters into shopping malls in China. The negative outlook reflects the likelihood that \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  will lower the corporate credit rating to "selective default". (jasper.moiseiwitsch@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0308 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] South Korea's weak industrial output in October and an expected fall in exports in November are increasing the chances for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut its policy rate again in December, says Nomura economist Kwon Young-sun. He says he "would not be surprised if \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  delivers a 25 basis point rate cut" to 1.75% when the BOK policy board meets on December 11 though he expects that rate cuts will likely be in January and April respectively next year. The BOK last cut its base rate in October to 2% to boost the economy. He expects the country's exports to have declined in November on weaker demand from China, Europe and Japan. The government said Friday the industrial output in October shrank a seasonally adjusted 1.6% from a month earlier after being flat in September. On a year-on-year basis, the output contracted 3.2% in October versus a 1.9% expansion the previous month. The readings are below market expectations for a 1% on-month growth and a 1.2% on-year contraction for October. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0302 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/IDR, like other regional USD/Asia pairs, has rallied on the back of USD/JPY's rebound but is struggling to overcome technical resistance at 12,190. The entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel may be key to more near-term U.S. dollar strength versus the rupiah. If USD/IDR ends Friday above 12,190, it could make its way to the top of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel at 12,380. But positive fundamental factors emerging for Indonesia--such as the government's aggressive budget-trimming and an inflation-fighting stance by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --could help the rupiah hold its own in the medium term. USD/IDR is now 12,195 from its Thursday close of 12,176. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0252 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indonesia stands out among Southeast Asian nations as the clear winner from a Japanese economic policy that tilts toward reflation, ANZ says. "Indonesia's exports are highly leveraged to Japan's domestic demand," ANZ economist Weiwen Ng writes in a research note, while low export similarity "suggests that Indonesia's exports do not necessarily compete with Japan's, avoiding loss of competitiveness relative to Japan's exports" in a time of a weaker yen. ANZ forecasts continued "protracted weakness in the yen" as the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loosens monetary policy to meet a 2% inflation goal, and suggests domestic demand will rise on the back of monetary and fiscal stimulus in addition to the "knock-on impact from an improvement in exports." (ben.otto@wsj.com; Twitter: @benottoWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0233 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China yuan falls as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guided the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker, and also because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened in the offshore market. The yuan is at 6.1456 versus 6.1392 at Thursday's close. The central parity is set at The USD/CNH, or offshore USD/CNY, is at 6.1545 versus 6.1482 late Thursday. "Investors aren't so bullish about the yuan any more and more importantly, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is allowing such fluctuations in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says a Shanghai-based local bank trader. Hu Xiaolian, a vice-governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said at a conference on Thursday that, following a widening of the trading band for the yuan, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has "basically exited from regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market." (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 27, 2014 22:36 ET (03:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141128eabs000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
