\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan holds steady as corporates cling to dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2014\par 06:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan was little changed\par on Thursday, with strong corporate demand for dollars\par counteracting the eight-and-a-half-month high midpoint set by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.  \par     By midday, spot yuan stood at 6.1392 per dollar, \par almost unchanged from Wednesday's close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the yuan's daily\par midpoint at 6.1320 per dollar, the highest level\par since March 17, up 0.06 percent from the previous day's fix. \par     Traders said corporates and individuals are keeping more \par dollars on hand as investors bet on further policy easing after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut benchmark interest rates last Friday. \par     Further easing could end the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rally of\par more than 2 percent against the dollar since May.\par     An index of the yuan's real effective exchange rate - the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value against a trade-weighted basket after\par adjustments based on inflation - showed an even more pronounced\par increase of 6.5 percent since May, according to the Bank for\par International Settements (BIS). \par     Latest BIS data shows the yuan index rose 1.5 percent to\par 117.73 in October from 115.99 in Sepetember. \par     Use of the renminbi also continues to rise, accounting for\par 11.2 percent of total payments between China and the rest of the\par world, state news agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xinhua\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported on Wednesday, citing\par Belgium-based global payment services company SWIFT. That's up\par from 6.2 percent 18 months ago. \par  \par     The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:  \par  Item                    Current      Previous     Change\par                                                    (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.132        6.1354       0.06%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan               6.1392       6.1389       0.00%\par  Divergence from         0.12%                     \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.39%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.81%\par  * Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 2 percent from\par the official midpoint rate it sets each morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\par     For the weekly CNH Tracker column, see: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ced53w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ced53w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                          Current      Difference\par                                                   from\par                                                   onshore\par                                                   (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan          (pct)   6.1468       -0.15%\par  Offshore non-deliverable forwards   6.251        -1.90%\par                                                   \par  * Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par ** Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par .     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACT