\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan inches up as \uc2 PBOC\uc2  sets midpoint at 8-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2014\par 05:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged up on\par Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the guidance rate at an\par eight-month high, signalling that policymakers don't intend to\par let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciate for now, traders said.  \par     By midday, spot yuan stood at 6.1344 per dollar,\par 0.03 percent firmer than Tuesday's close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the yuan's daily\par midpoint at 6.1354 per dollar, the highest level\par since mid-March, up 0.06 percent from the previous day's fix. \par     Despite the surprise interest rate cut last Friday that\par tempered bullish bets on the yuan, traders and economists\par believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  will attempt to preserve general exchange rate\par stability through the midpoint, to guard against the risk of a\par panic selloff in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par  \par     The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:  \par  Item                       Current     Previous   Change\par                                                    (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1354      6.139      0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1344      6.1365     0.03%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.02%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.31%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.92%\par  * Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from the official midpoint rate it sets\par each morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\par     For the weekly CNH Tracker column, see: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ced53w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ced53w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par     \par  Instrument                    Current      Difference\par                                             from\par                                             onshore\par                                             (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan            6.1391       -0.08%\par  (pct)                                      \par  Offshore non-deliverable      6.25         -1.83%\par  forwards                                   \par  * Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par ** Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par .     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band