\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan stays near midpoint on increasing market caution\b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2014\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan stuck close to the\par official guidance rate for a second day on Tuesday as investors\par weighed how the recent monetary easing might impact the exchange\par rate.\par     By midday, spot yuan had rebounded from early\par losses to stand at 6.1405 per dollar, 0.02 percent stronger than\par Monday's close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the yuan's daily\par midpoint at 6.1390 per dollar, up 0.05 percent from\par previous day's fix. \par     Traders and economists believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  will attempt to\par preserve general exchange rate stability through the midpoint,\par to risk setting off a panic depreciation, but the market may be\par preparing to start consistently pricing the yuan weaker than the\par midpoint.\par     On Tuesday, the yuan opened weaker than the official\par guidance rate for the first time since late September. It\par touched a nearly two-month low at one point, as appetite for the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  waned after Friday's surprise rate cut by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     "It means investors are generally lowering their\par expectations on a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for now," said a trader at a\par foreign bank in Shanghai. \par     The cautious sentiment has caused the spot rate and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's guidance rate to converge in the last two trading\par sessions, a relatively rare occurrence that can often signal a\par long-term shift in trends. \par     Some traders forecast that the yuan will appreciate during\par December and be at 6.11-6.12 to the dollar at year-end, a level\par that would mean some depreciation for the whole year.\par     But if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  follows up with further easing to reserve\par requirement ratios or interest rates, the yuan could enter a\par longer depreciation cycle, they said. \par \par     The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:  \par  Item                        Current   Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.139     6.142      0.05%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1405    6.1417     0.02%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   0.02%                \par  Spot change ytd                                  -1.41%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation               34.79%\par  \par * Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from the official midpoint rate it sets\par each morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\par     For the weekly CNH Tracker column, see: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ced53w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ced53w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:   \par  Instrument                 Current  Difference from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.1492   -0.14%\par           *                          \par  Offshore non-deliverable   6.254    -1.84%\par  forwards               **           \par  * Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par ** Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par .     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>  \par \par  (Reporting by Shanghai N