\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sliding yen, weak  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  PMI hit Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Sing dlr up with  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2014\par 09:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 20 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par fell on Thursday with the South Korean won near a 15-month low\par as the yen lost ground and a private survey of China's\par manufacturing sector increased worries about a slowdown in the\par world's second-largest economy.\par     The Singapore dollar rose as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par suspected by traders of supporting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won kept underperforming as it is seen more\par sensitive to the yen's weakness, given the competition between\par South Korea and Japan in exports markets.\par     Investors built up the largest short positions in the won\par since the 2008 global financial crisis in the last two weeks, a\par Reuters poll showed. \par     Taiwan's dollar ended local trade down 0.5 percent\par at 31.015 per U.S. dollar, its weakest since October 2010.\par     The Indonesian rupiah fell as investors took\par profits from its gains after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised interest\par rates and the government increased fuel price earlier this week.\par     The yen hit a seven-year low against the dollar and a\par six-year trough versus the euro as speculators rushed\par to carry trades funded by super-cheap liquidity from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0800 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.57         117.98       -0.50\par   Sing dlr        1.3033         1.3055       +0.17\par   Taiwan dlr      31.009         30.876       -0.43\par   Korean won     1115.07        1106.30       -0.79\par   Baht             32.83          32.81       -0.05\par   Peso             45.07          45.07       +0.00\par   Rupiah        12170.00       12145.00       -0.21\par   Rupee            62.11          61.96       -0.24\par   Ringgit         3.3610         3.3600       -0.03\par   Yuan            6.1244         6.1198       -0.08\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.57         105.28      -11.21\par   Sing dlr        1.3033         1.2632       -3.08\par   Taiwan dlr      31.009         29.950       -3.42\par   Korean won     1115.07        1055.40       -5.35\par   Baht             32.83          32.86       +0.10\par   Peso             45.07          44.40       -1.50\par   Rupiah        12170.00       12160.00       -0.08\par   Rupee            62.11          61.80       -0.50\par   Ringgit         3.3610         3.2755       -2.54\par   Yuan            6.1244         6.0539       -1.15\par  \par  (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-20T09:29:56.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141120eabk008ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
