\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar resumes rise vs yen,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  warning knocks Aussie\b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2014\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Yen sags as Nikkei rises on renewed election speculation\par \par \uc2 * RBA's Kent: \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken Aussie remains an option\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  data roughly in line with expectations, little reaction (Rewrites throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Shinichi Saoshiro\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The dollar edged back toward a seven-year high struck earlier this week against the yen, as speculation swirled that Japan's Prime Minister Shinzo Abe will call a snap election in December.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was up 0.2 percent at 115.74 yen, nearing the seven-year high of 116.11 yen notched on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the market, the Australian dollar slid after a \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it regards as overvalued.\par \par \uc2 The dominant factor in the market this week, however, has been talk of a snap election in Japan. Analysts reckon Abe would use a victory to implement a second round of reflationary policies and possibly delay a planned sales tax hike.\par \par \uc2 This has spurred a rally in Tokyo's Nikkei share average and weighed on the yen. The Nikkei fell earlier in Thursday's session but was up 1 percent, poised to mark its highest close in seven years.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen has been following domestic stocks recently as many participants, particularly foreign players, sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hedge their equities positions.\par \par \uc2 The yen's fall and the Nikkei's advance was slowed on Wednesday when a top government spokesman cooled speculation of Abe taking the sales tax issue to voters.\par \par \uc2 But the respite was cut short when a senior figure in Abe's ruling party told reporters it appeared the premier has decided to call an election.\par \par \uc2 Abe is widely expected to make his election decision depending on the strength of economic indicators, with third quarter gross domestic product data due to be released on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Policymaker comments are a bigger focus than data ahead of next week's GDP release," \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Todd Elmer said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The market also awaited U.S. data like jobless claims later in the session and retail sales data on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The numbers may reinforce perceptions that the U.S. economy is doing better than either Europe's or Japan's, raising the prospect of more policy divergence that has been helping to push the dollar higher against the euro and yen.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting an improving economy, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  ended its money-printing programme last month, while the BOJ boosted its stimulus measures to re-energise a fragile recovery. The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also under pressure to ease more and support a sluggish euro zone economy.\par \par \uc2 "The market was able to absorb stop-loss selling of the dollar when it broke below 115 yen overnight as bargain hunting soon emerged. With U.S. and Japanese monetary policies on divergent paths, participants are still poised to buy the dollar on dips," said Kaneo Ogino, director at Global-info Co in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 The euro was flat at $1.2444, confined to a narrow range and managing to stay clear of a two-year low of $1.2358 hit last week.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar was down 0.25 percent at $0.8699 after Reserve Bank of Australia Assistant Governor \uc2 Christopher Kent\uc2  repeated that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained an option.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie has fallen 2.5 percent against the dollar so far this year but the RBA had repeatedly said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was over-valued.\par \par \uc2 As China is Australia's main export market, the Australian dollar is sensitive to China's economic fortunes. But it showed little reaction to China's industrial output and retails sales figures, which were roughly in line with expectations. (Editing by \uc2 Simon Cameron-Moore\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-13T07:20:35.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141113eabd006f7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
