\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan nearly flat after \uc2 APEC\uc2  summit\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2014\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 13 (Reuters) - China's yuan barely moved\par against the dollar on Thursday as investors turn cautious after\par the conclusion of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 APEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  summit earlier this week, traders\par said.\par     China typically keeps its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steady or lets it\par appreciate moderately during major political events to deflect\par criticism that Beijing holds down the value of the yuan to bosst\par its export power.\par     Spot yuan traded at 6.1270 per dollar by midday,\par almost unchanged from the close on Wednesday when it touched a\par three-week low right after \f28 \uc2 \f2 APEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint at\par 6.1418, up a marginal 0.02 percent from Wednesday's fix.\par     Traders said the market is divided on the future trend,\par making the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's guidance crucial in the near term.\par    \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1418     6.1428       0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1270     6.1262       -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.24%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.19%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.08%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1344    -0.12%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2680    -2.01%\par  forwards               **                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlig