\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls to 3-week low on c.bank guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2014\par 04:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 12 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell to a\par three-week low against the dollar on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set another weaker midpoint. \par     Spot yuan traded at 6.1272 per dollar by midday,\par 0.03 percent weaker than the previous close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint at\par 6.1428, down 0.02 percent from Tuesday's fix.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to guide the Chinese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to depreciate in the near term amid the slowing\par economy. A weaker yuan will also help deter inflows of\par speculative hot money, which have seen a revival of late.\par  \par     \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1428     6.1413       -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1272     6.1252       -0.03%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.25%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.20%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.08%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument