\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan edges lower on weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2014\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell against the\par dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the midpoint\par slightly weak, signalling that Beijing may prefer a temporary\par pause for the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent appreciation, traders\par said.\par     Spot yuan traded at 6.1203 per dollar by midday,\par 0.01 percent weaker than the previous close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint at\par 6.1413, down 0.6 percent from Monday's fix.\par     The yuan has stayed on a general upward trend since May, \par appreciating 2.3 percent since the end of April, buoyed by\par China's strong foreign trade surpluses.\par     \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1413     6.1377       -0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1203     6.1196       -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.34%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.08%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.23%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\p