\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 10\b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par 07:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA CONSUMER INFLATION HOLDS STEADY -- UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer inflation held steady in October, allowing more room for monetary easing as growth momentum slips in the world's second-largest economy. (published 0330 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN LENDING TO PROPERTY INVESTORS RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lending to property investors in Australia rose in September, continuing an upward trend that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has expressed growing concern over. (published 0044 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S XI, JAPAN'S ABE MEET IN BEIJING: 2ND UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe held their first face-to-face discussions since both took power two years ago, a potential thaw in the relationship that has been frozen and veered close to open conflict in the past two years. (published 0516 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA, CHINA AGREE ON FREE TRADE DEAL -- UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leaders of China and South Korea have reached broad agreement on a bilateral free-trade deal, allowing Korean firms enhanced access to China's huge market and marking a diplomatic victory of sorts for Beijing. (published 0535 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA, CHINA CENTRAL BANKS SIGN PACT ON YUAN CLEARING ARRANGEMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday it has signed an initial agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  on yuan clearing arrangements in Malaysia. (published 0535 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABE, PUTIN AGREE TO IMPROVE TIES DESPITE SANCTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leaders of Japan and Russia agreed to continue deepening bilateral ties through a range of steps--including a visit by Russian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Japan next year--even as Tokyo faces pressure to cooperate further with Western nations in imposing sanctions over Moscow's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Ukraine. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO START STOCK TRADING LINK NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is set to open up Shanghai's stock market to investors overseas, granting access to invest in an estimated US$2 trillion of mainland equities, with the launch of a trading link between Hong Kong and Shanghai on Nov. 17. (published 0105 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CHINA RAILWAY CONSTRUCTION\f28 \uc2 \f2  TURNING TO LEGAL MEANS AFTER MEXICO DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Railway Construction Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it would resort to legal means to protect its interests after the Mexican government revoked a $4 billion deal with a Chinese-led consortium. (published 0419 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINSHENG BANK UNVEILS CAPITAL- RAISING PLANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Minsheng Banking\f28 \uc2 \f2  Corp.plans to sell 38 billion yuan in preferred shares to domestic and overseas investors and ordinary stock to its employees, in a bid to boost its capital amid a rapid expansion of its business. (published 0520 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KEPPEL UNIT TO TEST MARKET APPETITE FOR IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Keppel Telecommunications\f28 \uc2 \f2  & Transport Ltd. will start testing investor appetite this week for an over 500 million Singapore dollar initial public offering of its data centers, people with knowledge of the deal said Monday. (published 0148 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAPITALAND: TO MANAGE FIVE MORE APARTMENT PROPERTIES IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Southeast Asia's largest property developer by market value, said Monday that it has secured contracts to manage five more apartment properties in China, bringing the total number of apartment units it manages in the country to more than 12,000. (published 0133 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIRASIA X: SLOWED PACE OF CAPACITY GROWTH TO PROTECT MARGINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AirAsia X Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the long-haul associate of Malaysian discount carrier \f28 \uc2 \f2 AirAsia Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Monday said it has slowed capacity growth to protect its margins after it added seven aircraft to its fleet over the last year. (published 0445 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CHINA RESOURCES LAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : CHAIRMAN RESIGNS DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Resources Land Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a Chinese property developer, said Monday that its chairman, Wu Xiangdong, resigned due to personal reasons. (published 0201 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MIZUHO BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  KEEPS LONG-TERM PRIME RATE AT 1.15% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it set its long-term prime lending rate for November at 1.15%, unchanged from October. (published 0333 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BDO UNIBANK, KOREA EXIMBANK EXPAND CREDIT LINE TO $700 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BDO Unibank Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has expanded a credit line agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 , giving Korean firms access to $500 million in fresh funds to expand their businesses in the Philippines. (published 0529 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONG KONG LEADS ASIAN SHARES HIGHER -- UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks in Hong Kong surged Monday, leading most of the region higher, after news that a highly-anticipated trading link between Hong Kong and Shanghai will start next week. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL EDGES UP ON POSITIVE CHINA ECONOMIC, OIL DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures rose in Asian trade Monday on the back of positive Chinese economic data, but gains were limited as oil markets remained focused on production levels from the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting countries. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 10, 2014 01:09 ET (06:09 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141110eaba000ky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
