\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan edges up on stronger midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par 05:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Nov 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose against the\par dollar on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the midpoint to its\par strongest level since mid-March. \par     Spot yuan traded at 6.1141 per dollar by midday,\par 0.14 percent firmer from the previous close.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint at\par 6.1377, up 0.4 percent from Friday's fix to its strongest level\par since March 19. \par     China released October trade data during the weekend, but\par the official Shanghai Securities News said on Monday that the\par export figures pointed to signs of manipulation and inflows of\par speculative hot money.  \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1377     6.1602       0.37%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1141     6.1229       0.14%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.38%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -0.98%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.37%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore 