\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan flat despite a two-month low midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2014\par 04:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Nov 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan was flat against\par the dollar on Thursday, though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened the\par official midpoint to the lowest level in two months.\par     Spot yuan traded at 6.1149 per dollar near\par midday, almost no change from the previous day's close at\par 6.1146. It changed hands between 6.1146 and 6.1161 in morning\par trade.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint at\par 6.1565, down 0.1 percent from Wednesday's 6.1503. It's the\par weakest level since Sept 4.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1565     6.1503       -0.10%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1149     6.1146       0.00%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.68%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.00%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.35%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current   Difference from\par                                           onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          