\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slide,  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  concerns hurt Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2014\par 06:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution grows, won at 6-year high vs\par yen\par     * Foreigners cut Malaysian bond holdings in September\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 3 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the\par Malaysian ringgit led losses in emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Monday as the yen extended slides amid more evidence of slowing\par growth in China's economy.\par     The won fell to its weakest in more than seven\par months against the dollar as caution grew over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to check its\par strength against the yen. The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par earlier touched a six-year high versus the Japanese unit.\par     The ringgit hit a near nine-month low on data\par showing foreigners in September cut bond holdings and on dollar\par demand linked to the daily fixing. Indonesia's rupiah \par eased on a contraction in manufacturing activity.\par     The yen fell to a fresh seven-year low against the\par dollar, extending losses after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's surprise\par decision to increase bond-buying stimulus on Friday.\par  The dollar hit a four-year peak against a\par basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Asia Pacific shares outside Japan eased as China's factory\par activity fell to a five month-low in October, reinforcing\par worries that the growth outlook remains murky. A\par separate private survey showed service grew at its slowest pace\par in nine months last month. \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have many bearish factors such as a strong\par dollar and weak China data for a short term," said Yuna Park, a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "Still, they may rebound once expectations of carry trades\par revive."\par     Investors are keeping an eye out on whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday follows the BOJ's decision.\par     \par     WON\par     The won lost as much as 1.0 percent to 1,079.8 per dollar,\par its weakest since March 25.\par     Caution grew over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the won gained 0.6 percent\par to 9.4890 against the yen, its strongest since August 2008.\par     The authorities had been spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the won\par was around 9.5000 yen, traders said. South Korean and Japanese\par companies compete head-on for a similar group of products on\par major markets around the world.\par     "Given the export similarity across these economies, there\par will be concerns that this easing will hamper exports in Korea\par and Taiwan," \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note, referring to the BOJ's policy\par stimulus on Friday.\par     "A weaker JPY could see such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases by local central\par banks accelerate from here."\par     South Korea's manufacturing activity suffered its worst\par decline in four months in October and its outlook even bleaker\par as new export orders fell, a private survey showed earlier.\par  \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell as much as 0.7 percent to 3.3110 per\par dollar, its weakest since Feb. 14.\par     Foreign investors reduced holdings in the country's debt\par securities by 7.6 billion ringgit ($2.3 billion) in September to\par 249.3 billion ringgit, according to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also fell against the neighbouring\par Singapore dollar.\par     Investors stayed cautious over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with agent banks spotted in\par the market, traders said.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0440 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       112.70         112.31       -0.35\par   Sing dlr        1.2868         1.2863       -0.04\par   Taiwan dlr      30.482         30.478       -0.01\par   Korean won     1073.10        1068.50       -0.43\par   Baht             32.61          32.56       -0.15\par   Peso             44.98          44.88       -0.22\par   Rupiah        12096.00       12080.00       -0.13\par   Rupee            61.45          61.40       -0.09\par   Ringgit         3.3085         3.2893       -0.58\par   Yuan            6.1171         6.1135       -0.06\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       112.70         105.28       -6.59\par   Sing dlr        1.2868         1.2632       -