\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan eases as dollar gains globally on \uc2 Fed\uc2 's hawkish tone\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2014\par 05:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 30 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell against the\par dollar on Thursday after rising in the previous four trading\par sessions, tracking a weaker midpoint fixing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par as the greenback strengthened in international markets.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the midpoint rate at\par 6.1457 per dollar, down 0.08 percent from the previous fix, as\par the dollar index surged after the Wednesday's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  meeting.  \par     The dollar stayed on the front foot on Thursday, hovering\par near 3-1/2 week highs against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised markets with a more hawkish policy\par tone and signaled its confidence in the U.S. economic\par recovery. \par     The spot market opened at 6.1148 yuan per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1136 by midday, 0.05 percent weaker from the\par previous close.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                    Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.1457       6.1405       -0.08%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan               6.1141       6.1112       -0.05%\par  Divergence from         -0.52%                    \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -0.98%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.38%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                          Current      Difference\par                                                   from\par                                                   onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *       6.1189       -0.09%\par  Offshore non-deliverable forwards   6.2365       -1.46%\par                **                                 \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Simon\par Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-30T05:23:21.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141030eaau003yd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
