\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan touches 7-1/2 month high on stronger midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2014\par 05:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 29 (Reuters) - China's yuan climbed to a 7-1/2\par month high against the dollar on Wednesday, appreciating for the\par third straight session after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again set a\par stronger midpoint. \par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit 6.1092 per dollar in early trade,\par its highest level since March.\par     It trimmed some gains by midday to change hands at 6.1117, \par up 0.03 percent from Tuesday's close.\par     Before the market opened, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed the midpoint rate at 6.1405 per dollar, up 0.03 percent\par from the previous fix.  Wednesday was the third consecutive day\par on which the midpoint was fixed at a stronger level.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                    Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.1405       6.1421       0.03%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan               6.1117       6.1133       0.03%\par  Divergence from         -0.47%                    \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -0.95%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.42%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                          Current      Difference\par                                                   from\par                                                   onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *       6.1133       -0.03%\par  Offshore non-deliverable forwards   6.2325       -1.48%\par                **                                 \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 