\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan firms on stronger midpoint, seen rising ahead of \uc2 APEC\uc2  summit\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2014\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose against the\par dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set another stronger\par midpoint.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to let the Chinese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continue a steady but slow appreciation ahead of the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 summit next month.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1421\par per dollar prior to market open on Tuesday, up 0.04 percent from\par the previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1162 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1139 by midday, 0.05 percent firmer from the\par previous close.\par     Asia-Pacific leaders will meet for a summit in Beijing on\par Nov. 10 and 11 among other \f28 \uc2 \f2 APEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  activities around that time.\par China typically lets its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain steady or rise\par moderately during major political events. Traders say it is to \par deflect criticism that Beijing holds down the value of the yuan\par for competitive advantage.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                    Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.1421       6.1446       0.04%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan               6.1139       6.1167       0.05%\par  Divergence from         -0.46%                    \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -0.98%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.37%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                          Current      Difference\par                                                   from\par                                                   onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *       6.1183       -0.07%\par  Offshore non-deliverable forwards   6.233        -1.46%\par                **                                 \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capita