\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan hits 7-mnth high for second straight session on c.bank guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2014\par 04:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose against the\par dollar on Monday, hitting its highest level since March for the\par second trading day in a row, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its\par official guidance rate firmer. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1446\par per dollar prior to market open, up 0.03 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1140 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1156 by midday, 0.03 percent firmer from the\par previous close.\par     The yuan has rallied since late September, hitting a slew of\par multi-month highs last week, buoyed by China's strong trade\par surpluses every month since May, which have increased dollar\par supply in the market.\par         \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1446       6.1467       0.03%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1156       6.1172       0.03%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.47%                    \par  Spot change ytd                                      -1.01%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                   35.33%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets 