\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-China's capital outflows not a risk, in line with reforms - regulator\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2014\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Decline in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in line with policy goals               \par \par \uc2 * Decline attributable to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, especially dollar               \par \par \uc2 * Sees signs of increased volatility in cross-border flows               \par \par \uc2 * Will develop more derivatives for firms to better hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk   (Adds quotes, details)               \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Oct 23 (Reuters) - China's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator is not concerned by signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows as the economy slows, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said on Thursday, saying a recent decline in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves is in line with Beijing's policy goals.               \par \par \uc2 China is closely monitoring the impact of any changes in U.S. monetary policy, amid signs of greater volatility in cross-border flows, said Guan Tao, head of the department of international payments at \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE).               \par \par \uc2 "Capital inflows are swinging into outflows due to recent two-way fluctuations in the yuan exchange rate and the complex external and internal environment, which is normal," Guan told a news conference. "Such capital outflows are not risky."               \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's largest, fell by about $100 billion in the third quarter to $3.89 trillion at the end of September, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.               \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the decline suggested speculative "hot money" outflows from China amid increased market jitters about whether the world's second-largest economy may be at risk of a sharper slowdown.               \par \par \uc2 Guan said the decline in reserves was mainly caused by a recent rise in the U.S. dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reduces the dollar value of the proportion of the reserves held in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "The slowdown in growth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will become a new normal and is in line with the direction of reforms," he said.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is gradually exiting from regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he added.               \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vast factory sector grew a shade faster in October as firms drew more foreign and domestic orders, a private survey showed earlier on Thursday, but analysts say the modest expansion does not indicate a turnaround for the cooling Chinese economy.               \par \par \uc2 Data this week showed China's annual economic growth slowed to 7.3 percent in the third quarter - the weakest pace since the depths of the global financial crisis, from 7.5 percent in the previous quarter.               \par \par \uc2 China's officials have pledge to rebalance trade to help slow down the build-up of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which could complicate monetary policy and stoke inflation in the long term.               \par \par \uc2 The government will further develop derivative instruments to help companies better hedge against two-way volatility in the yuan exchange rate, Guan added.               \par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubled the yuan's daily trading band against the dollar in a bid to introduce two-way swings in the yuan, hitting investors who bet on its continued rise.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-23T06:05:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141023eaan002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
