\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls slightly on weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2014\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan dipped against the\par dollar on Thursday, retreating from a seven-month high hit a day\par earlier after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official guidance rate\par weaker.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1459\par per dollar prior to market open, down 0.04 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1183 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1193 by midday, down 0.01 percent from the\par previous close.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been posting steady gains since late\par September on the back of China's improved trade data.\par     Many traders forecast the uptrend will continue, with the\par yuan having the potential to rise above the 6.1 per dollar\par level. \par     A private survey on Thursday showed that China's vast\par factory sector grew a shade faster in October as firms saw more\par foreign and domestic orders, but the modest expansion was not\par seen signifying a turnaround for the slowing\par economy. \par     Traders noted that the survey had no immediate impact on\par yuan trading.\par     \par     The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                    Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.1459       6.1437       -0.04%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan               6.1193       6.1185       -0.01%\par  Divergence from         -0.43%                    \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.07%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.25%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                    Current      Difference\par                                             from\par                                             onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan            6.1254       -0.10%\par  *                                          \par  Offshore non-deliverable      6.245        -1.59%\par  forwards               **                  \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DA