\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan hits seven-month high on strong midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2014\par 06:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 16 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged\par up against dollar on Thursday, buoyed by a strong midpoint\par fixing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and continuing an appreciation trend\par that started in late September. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit the seven-month high at 6.1209 per dollar \par in early trade but trimmed some gains by midday after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   posted September credit data.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set its midpoint rate \par up 0.1 percent at 6.1395 per dollar in response to a 0.8 percent\par weakening of the dollar index in global markets\par overnight.\par     That was the Chinese official rate's strongest level since\par mid-March when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doubled the yuan/dollar trading\par band to 2 percent. \par     The spot market opened at 6.1259 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1240 by midday, 0.03 percent firmer than the\par previous close.\par     Chinese banks made 857.2 billion yuan worth of new loans in\par September, data showed on Thursday, beating market expectations\par in a sign that demand for credit may be picking up.\par  \par     But overall credit data last month remained lacklustre, a\par sign of a lingering growth slowdown in the world's\par second-largest economy, traders said.\par         \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                     Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint            6.1395       6.1455       +0.10%\par                                                     \par  Spot yuan                6.1240       6.1259       +0.03%\par  Divergence from          -0.25%                    \par  midpoint*                                          \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.14%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.15%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                      Current      Difference\par                                               from\par                                               onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1371       -0.21%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.2420       -1.64%\par  forwards               **                    \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highli