\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls slightly on weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2014\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan \par retreated from a seven-month high against the dollar on\par Wednesday, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official rate lower. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set its midpoint rate at\par 6.1455 per dollar prior to market open, down 0.08 percent from\par the previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1256 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1260 by midday, 0.02 percent weaker than the\par previous close.\par     China's September inflation cooled to a near five-year low,\par underscoring concerns that global growth is slowing fast, but\par the data earlier on Wednesday had no immediate impact on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said. \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                     Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint            6.1455       6.1408       -0.08%\par                                                     \par  Spot yuan                6.1260       6.1247       -0.02%\par  Divergence from          -0.32%                    \par  midpoint*                                          \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.18%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.10%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the 