\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan hits highest level since March on c.bank guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2014\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose to\par a seven-month high against the dollar on Tuesday, buoyed by a\par stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  midpoint.\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in a narrow range after hitting\par 6.1230 per dollar, the spot rate's highest level since early\par March.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been rallying slowly but steadily since\par late September on the back of strong trade data. \par      \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set its midpoint rate at\par 6.1408 per dollar prior to market open, up 0.06 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1259 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1239 at midday, 0.03 percent firmer than the\par previous close.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                     Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint            6.1408       6.1446       0.06%\par                                                     \par  Spot yuan                6.1239       6.1259       0.03%\par  Divergence from          -0.28%                    \par  midpoint*                                          \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.14%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.15%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                      Current      Difference\par                                               from\par                                               onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1348       -0.18%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.2400       -1.59%\par  forwards               **                    \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar