\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises on strong trade data, c.bank midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2014\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Oct 13 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the\par dollar on Monday, posting a nearly two-week high, after China\par released better-than-expected trade data for September and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed its official rate stronger.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set its midpoint rate at 6.1446\par per dollar prior to market open, up 0.04 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1315 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1266 at midday, 0.07 percent firmer from the\par previous close.\par     China's exports rose more than expected in September while\par imports unexpectedly improved, data showed on Monday, bringing\par the trade surplus to $31 billion. \par  \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                     Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint            6.1446       6.1470       0.04%\par                                                     \par  Spot yuan                6.1266       6.1309       0.07%\par  Divergence from          -0.29%                    \par  midpoint*                                          \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.19%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.09%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 