\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips ahead of likely weak data\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2014\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Oct 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan slipped on Friday\par as investors consolidated gains in a holiday-shortened week\par ahead of a raft of data next week which will provide clues on\par the extent of the slowdown in the economy.\par     Softer domestic demand probably pulled down growth in\par China's imports, investment and retail sales to multi-month or\par multi-year lows in September, raising questions about whether\par policymakers should do more to stimulate activity.\par  \par     "We expect below-consensus readings for all of these\par indicators, which would re-ignite growth concerns and exert some\par downward pressure on the yuan," said Dariusz Kowalczyk, a\par strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a daily note.\par     A weak midpoint fixing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also prompted\par some traders to take profits after recent gains on concerns\par about waning global growth.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1470\par per dollar prior to market open, slightly weaker than the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1300 per dollar, slightly\par stronger than Thursday's close but weakened to 6.1333 in late\par morning trades.\par     Concerns about weak Chinese data also weighed on the\par offshore yuan market where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened after posting\par strong gains this week. \par     As a result, the gap between the offshore and the onshore\par yuan narrowed substantially to below 80 pips from a high of\par nearly 400 pips seen at end September when pro-democracy\par protests intensified in Hong Kong.\par     A Reuters poll released on Thursday showed sentiment toward\par the yuan in the last two weeks remained bullish as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's\par Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  was generally setting official guidance rates at \par stronger levels. Still, long positions in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declined\par to their smallest since mid-July. \par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint             6.147       6.1461      -0.01%\par  Spot yuan                 6.1329      6.1305      -0.04%\par  Divergence from           -0.23%                  \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.29%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.95%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET    \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                      Current     Difference\par                                              from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1410      -0.03%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.234       -1.40%\par  forwards               **                   \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by Saik