\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises for 2nd day on stronger midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2014\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Oct 9 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose for a second\par consecutive day against the dollar on Thursday, after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official guidance rate stronger, signaling\par its comfort with a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for now.      \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1461\par per dollar prior to market open, slightly stronger from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1330 per dollar, up 0.1 percent\par from the previous close, and was changing hands at 6.1342 in\par late morning trades.\par     The spot rate was trading slightly stronger than the\par midpoint fixing in line with recent trends. \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                    Current     Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint           6.1461      6.1493      0.05%\par                                                  \par  Spot yuan               6.134       6.139       0.08%\par  Divergence from         -0.20%                  \par  midpoint*                                       \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.31%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.93%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current     Difference\par                                             from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1349      0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2275      -1.31%\par  forwards               **                  \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performanc