\par\par \b \uc2 HK Protests Trigger Biggest Yuan Drop in 3 Months -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2014\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0244 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yuan extends losses after it recorded its biggest daily drop in more than three months Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains weak in the offshore market and month-end corporate dollar purchases continue. The yuan is at 6.1523 to a dollar, versus the 6.1501 level seen at Monday's close. The central parity is set at 6.1525 versus 6.1539 Monday. "It's good that the market will closed for a week from Wednesday--we will see a more clear picture about Hong Kong when we come back," says a Shanghai-based trader at a foreign bank, adding that the dollar-yuan may fall below the 6.1400 level if the protests end during the holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yuan's fall accelerates after the holiday, he adds. The USD/CNH, or the offshore yuan, is at 6.1747 versus 6.1678 late Monday. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY non-deliverable forwards are down at 6.2665/6.2690 from 6.2680/6.2734 late Monday. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor JSM\par \par \uc2 (Delayed by 1 hour)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 30-09-14 0400GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140930ea9u0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
