\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan steady, c.bank sets midpoint at two-week low\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2014\par 05:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan held steady\par against the dollar on Thursday though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the\par lowest official midpoint in more than two weeks.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at 6.1497 per\par dollar, down 0.06 percent from the previous fix. It was the\par weakest level since Sept. 9.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1353 near midday, down 0.01\par percent from Wednesday's close at 6.1346. \par     The yuan traded at a narrow range between 6.1344 and 6.1372\par in morning trade.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:            \par  Item                       Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1497     6.1462       -0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1353     6.1346       -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.23%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.33%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 34.90%\par  * Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:           \par  Instrument                     Current  Difference from\par                                          onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1418   -0.03%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.234    