\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan steady, better-than-expected PMI survey no impact\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2014\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan was little\par changed against the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set\par a very marginally stronger official guidance rate.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at 6.1470 per\par dollar, up 0.02 percent from the previous fix. \par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1399 near midday, up 0.01\par percent from Monday's close at 6.1404. \par      Activity in China's manufacturing sector unexpectedly\par picked up in September even as factory employment slumped to a\par 5-1/2-year low, a survey showed, but it had no impact on the\par spot market. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 /Markit Flash China Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI)\par rose to 50.5 in September from August's final reading of 50.2.\par  \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:         \par  Item                       Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.147      6.1485      0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1399     6.1404      0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.12%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.40%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.80%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current    Difference from\par                                            onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1464     0.11%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2375     -1.45%\par  forwards               **                 \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrsl