\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises on midpoint, seen moving between 6.13-15 in near term\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2014\par 07:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 19 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against\par the dollar on Friday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a marginally\par stronger midpoint, leaving the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  little changed on the\par week.\par     Traders said they suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had moved to\par support the yuan this week as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared under\par pressure of depreciation because of the dollar's strength in\par global markets, China's slowing economic growth and signs of\par capital outflows from the country.\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.1381 per dollar by midday,\par up 0.04 percent from Thursday's close, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank\par of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set its official midpoint at 6.1455, or 0.06\par percent firmer from Thursday's close.\par     "We believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in the market to defend\par  the yuan's value after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  statement this week," said a\par trader at an Asian bank in Shanghai.\par     The U.S. Federal Reserve on Wednesday renewed its pledge to\par keep interest rates near zero for a "considerable time",\par signalling the global strength of dollar may linger in\par the near term. \par     Some traders said weak sentiment towards the yuan prevailed\par as both domestic and international investors are concerned about\par the health of the world's second-largest economy after August\par data pointed to further softness.\par     "It is now necessary for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take some\par measures to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilising," said a trader at a\par European bank in Shanghai.\par     Therefore, traders forecast the yuan will move in the range\par of 6.13-6.15 in the near term until China's economic picture\par brightens. \par     \par     SIGNS OF CAPITAL OUTFLOWS\par     The current economic downtrend has also influenced the\par country's cross-border capital flows.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and commercial banks sold 31.1 billion\par yuan ($5 billion) worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a net basis in\par August, according to a Reuters calculation based on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par data released on Monday. \par     The sales came after China reported a record high foreign\par trade surplus in August, signalling possible capital outflows\par from China, traders said.\par     Growth fears have deterred capital inflows into China, a\par research note by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Communications\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\par     However, Shen Danyang, China's trade ministry spokesman,\par said on Tuesday that China saw no obvious outflows of foreign\par capital. \par      \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                        Current     Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1455      6.149      0.06%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1381      6.1406     0.04%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.12%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.37%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 34.84%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                      Current      Difference\par                                               from\par                                               onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1419       -0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.234        -1.42%\par  forwards               **                    \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-19T06:07:38.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140919ea9j002zw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
