\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan edges down on weak midpoint and FDI data\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2014\par 06:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 16 (Reuters) - China's yuan softened against\par the dollar on Tuesday for the fourth straight day after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker midpoint and in response to weak\par foreign direct investment (FDI) figures.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at\par 6.1462 per dollar prior to market open, down 0.02 percent from\par the previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     Spot yuan opened at 6.1501 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1481 by midday, down 0.10 percent from the\par previous close. \par     China drew $78.3 billion in FDI in the first eight months of\par 2014, down 1.8 percent from a year earlier. In August alone, the\par figure was $7.2 billion, down 14 percent from a year earlier,\par and at a level not seen in at least 2-1/2 years. \par     Increasing risk of an export slowdown was also seen weighing\par on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     Shen Danyang, trade ministry spokesman, said on Tuesday that\par China's exports may not be able to sustain high growth in the\par months to come although the country's trade situation was\par stabilising. \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                      Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint             6.1462       6.1452       -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                 6.1481       6.1420       -0.10%\par  Divergence from           0.03%                     \par  midpoint*                                           \par  Spot change ytd                                     -1.53%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.62%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                           Current     Difference\par                                                   from\par                                                   onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *        6.1621      -0.23%\par  Offshore non-deliverable forwards    6.2385      -1.48%\par                **                                 \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - The yuan resumes appreciating on a trade-weighted basis\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Jacqueline\par Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-16T05:11:15.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140916ea9g003bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
