\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls vs dlr on weaker-than-expected factory data\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2014\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened against\par the dollar on Monday as growth fears deepened after the release\par of China's factory output data over the weekend, offsetting a\par firmer midpoint set by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     China's factory output grew at the weakest pace in nearly\par six years in August while growth in other key sectors also\par cooled. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate at\par 6.1452 per dollar prior to market open, up 0.03 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     But the yuan's spot rate was changing hands at\par 6.1387 by midday, down 0.07 percent from the previous close.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1452       6.1468       0.03%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1387       6.1346       -0.07%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.11%                    \par  Spot change ytd                                      -1.38%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                   34.82%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current      Difference\par                                              from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1458       -0.12%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.232        -1.39%\par  forwards               **                   \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http