\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan falls slightly on c.bank guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2014\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Sept 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell slightly\par against the dollar on Thursday, guided by a weaker midpoint set\par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reflect strength in the global dollar\par index.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixed the midpoint at 6.1453 per\par dollar prior to market open, down 0.05 percent from the previous\par day's 6.1425. \par     The spot market changed hands at 6.1315 near midday, down\par 0.03 percent from Wednesday's close at 6.1299. \par     The yuan's spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent\par above or below the midpoint.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:            \par  Item                        Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1453     6.1425      -0.05%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1315     6.1299      -0.03%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.22%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.27%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 34.98%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                 Current   Difference from\par                                       onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.1358    -0.04%\par           *                     