\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan drops on c.bank guidance, set to end flat for week\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2014\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan declined against\par the dollar on Friday due to a weaker midpoint fix and is set to\par end flat for the week, as markets await the release of August\par trade data. \par     Spot yuan stood at 6.1411 by midday, 0.04 percent\par softer from Thursday's close, almost unchanged on the week. \par     On Friday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the\par midpoint rate at 6.1707 per dollar, down 0.07 percent from the\par previous fix, reflecting the sharp rise of the U.S. index on\par Thursday.\par     The U.S. dollar posted an over 1 percent rise overnight\par after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates on Thursday.\par  \par     The market is expecting the release of trade data for August\par to shed light on the direction of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with\par some positive expectations slowly driving up the yuan recently,\par traders said.\par     "If the August's trade surplus continued to be good, it\par would definitely add more pressure to the yuan's appreciation in\par the coming months," said a trader at an Asian bank in Shanghai. \par     A Reuters poll projected August trade surplus would be $40\par billion, slightly down from July's historical high $47.3\par billion.  \par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                        Current     Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1707      6.1666      -0.07%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1411      6.1386      -0.04%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.48%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                     -1.42%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.77%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current      Difference\par                                              from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1450       -0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.226        -0.89%\par  forwards               **                   \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint afte