\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises despite daily midpoint fix at 3-mth low\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2014\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 3 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against due\par to dollar sales by corporates on  Wednesday, though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had fixed its daily guidance level at a three-month low.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1697\par yuan per dollar prior to market open, its weakest level since\par June 3, down 0.02 percent from the previous fix, reflecting the\par dollar's strength in global markets. \par     The yuan's spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent\par above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1469 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1449 by midday, 0.06 percent firmer from the\par previous close.\par     The premium of the spot rate against the midpoint widened to\par 0.40 percent from 0.37 percent at midday on Tuesday, indicating\par a divergence in views between the market and regulators.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current      Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1697       6.1684       -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1449       6.1488       0.06%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.40%                    \par  Spot change ytd                                      -1.48%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                   34.69%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current      Difference from\par                                              onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1486       -0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2260       -0.90%\par  forwards               **                   \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub -\par China c.banker \par - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performan