\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan marginally lower, following c.bank guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2014\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 2 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened\par marginally against the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par set its guidance rate slightly lower.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at 6.1684 per\par dollar before the market opened, down 0.01 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1441 per dollar and the yuan was\par changing hands at 6.1455 by midday, down 0.04 percent from the\par previous close.\par     The spread between the spot rate and midpoint has widened in\par recent trading days, a result of the spot market staying flat\par even though the bank has pushed down the midpoint rate,\par indicating divergence in views between the market and\par regulators.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                      Current       Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint             6.1684        6.1680    -0.01%\par  Spot yuan                 6.1455        6.1428    -0.04%\par  Divergence from           -0.37%                  \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.49%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.68%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                      Current       Difference\par                                                from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *   6.1487        -0.05%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.2275        -0.95%\par  forwards               **                     \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/req62w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/req62w}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fld