\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan almost unchanged after moving in narrow range\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2014\par 05:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan was barely changed\par against the dollar on Thursday, moving in a narrow range after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily midpoint rate nearly flat.\par     Traders said the generally flat midpoint fixings of late\par signalled the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's intention to hold the yuan steady, as\par growth of the world's second-largest economy appears to be\par faltering again.  \par     On Thursday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the\par midpoint rate at 6.1638 per dollar prior to market open, up 0.03\par percent from the previous fix. The spot rate is currently\par allowed to trade 2 percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1420 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1425 at midday, only 0.01 percent firmer\par from the previous close.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1638     6.1658    0.03%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1425     6.1432    0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.35%               \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.44%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.74%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET 