\par\par \b \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 : China Effect Will Keep Rates Low -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2014\par 17:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:51 EDT - Need more reasons to expect interest rates will stay low for longer? \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  reminds us of the uberforce which drove them lower in the first place: \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 , export-driven economic model. Its London-based economics team recaps a decade of the "Revived Bretton Woods System" in which China and other emerging-market countries bought dollars--the primary reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as with official Bretton Woods arrangement--to depress their exchange rates. That led them to accumulate Treasurys and other US assets, driving down interest rates. Although China is gradually changing its economic model, it continues to accumulate reserves, and \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  argues the country's rising economic size will amplify the reserve growth. Combined with India's move toward export-driven growth, the development could "reload a new driver of low interest rates." (michael.casey@wsj.com; @mikejcasey)\par \par \uc2 11:50 EDT - \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 ' Eric Green says it's entirely possible that if the ECB takes additional action to spur growth, it will push the \uc2 Fed\uc2  to be more aggressive with its eventual campaign of interest rate increases. The issue is the overall level of liquidity around the world and the level of interest rates in the global financial system, he says. "A US term structure that suffers a gravitational tug owing to overseas events is likely to affect the cost/benefit calculus of policy," Green writes. "Assuming recent economic trends persist, low rates and global liquidity that will remain ample or even rise after [ECB] QE3 could encourage the \uc2 Fed\uc2  to tighten policy sooner rather than later." (michael.derby@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1546 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  expects the ECB to take additional easing steps next week but stop short of QE. In a research note, the bank said it expects the ECB to reduce all of its interest rates by 10 basis points, which would leave the main refinancing rate at 0.05% and the deposit rate at -0.2%. The ECB may also remove the 10 basis point premium it has added to the interest rate on four-year loans that will be offered to banks starting next month. "This means that banks will be able to lock in even more funding for up to four years at an even lower interest rate of just 0.05%," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  economist \uc2 Greg Fuzesi\uc2  wrote. The ECB may also give more details on its plans to purchase asset-backed securities. As for QE, "we think that the likelihood has increased to almost 50% next year and that it is now over 30% by year-end," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1535 GMT As the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues its efforts to revive Europe's asset-backed securities markets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  latest numbers on European structured finance defaults show why policy makers have shifted from fearing ABS to embracing it. In the seven years since the financial crisis broke out, just 1.6%, or EUR43.5 billion, of European structured notes outstanding then have defaulted, \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes. By contrast, the rate for the U.S. is 19.3%, equivalent to $1.1 trillion. Moreover, just under two-thirds of European notes' ratings have remained stable or risen since mid-2007, \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  says, while close to 70% of the notes outstanding then have been redeemed. (richard.barley@wsj.com; @RichardBarley1) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:31 EDT - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  watchers attempting to get a sense of where inflation lies are frequently vexed by the different way price pressures are measured. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it's targeting 2% as measured by the PCE index, but that gauge is somewhat obscure compared to the widely known \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which tends to run a bit hotter. That can create challenges for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  as it seeks to explain where it is relative to its price goal. Researchers at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cleveland Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  argue in a new paper that a variation of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2 , called the chained \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2 , more closely tracks the PCE price index. They add that the chained \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2  "shows some recent progress toward the FOMC's longer-run inflation goal of 2%." (michael.derby@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1519 GMT Austrian Vice Chancellor and Finance Minister Michael Spindelegger's resignation have increased the risk of new elections in the Alpine country which could have negative effects on Austrian government bonds, \f28 \uc2 \f2 DZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Analyst Daniel Lenz says. His "resignation could...unleash a major government crisis," Mr. Lenz says. New elections would most likely play into the hands of Austria's right-wing, populist Freedom Party. Should a political vacuum be created by Mr. Spindelegger's departure or a new European-critical government come into power, under Freedom Party leadership, this would raise the likelihood of a tangible market reaction, Mr. Lenz says. "Should public discussion continue over the possibility of new elections, [Austrian government bonds] could be in for some stormy times." (nicole.lundeen@wsj.com; @nicole_Lundeen) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:19 EDT - Brazil's center-south region, which produces about 90% of the top-growing country's cane, will produce 545.9M metric tons in the current 2014-2015 season, down 5.9% from an earlier forecast, according to Brazilian sugar cane industry group Unica. But sugar output is still up 6.4% during the season through the first half of August, and the global sugar market is likely to register a surplus of 1.306M metric tons for the season, according to the latest outlook from the London-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Sugar Organization\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Any possible price recovery brought by production shocks over the course of 2014-2015 might be muted by the huge stocks accumulated since the beginning of the surplus phase in 2010-11," ISO says. Raw sugar for October delivery recently up 1.2% at 15.55c/lb. (alexandra.wexler@wsj.com; @alexandrawexler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:10 EDT - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kroll Bond Rating Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  is helping invigorate a corner of the bond market that scarcely existed six months ago: small-bank debt. Six deals using a Kroll rating have been sold to investors this year, totaling $588.2M, the WSJ reports. It's a tiny drop in this year's $399B in financial company debt, but Kroll says there's potential for another dozen or so deals this year. These small banks pay higher yields than larger firms, attracting strong demand from investors. \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  are stepping up outreach in this nascent space. (timothy.martin@wsj.com; @timothywmartin)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1508 GMT Puma Energy, the oil storage and fuel distribution company spun out of commodities trading giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Trafigura Beheer B.V\f28 \uc2 \f2 . last year, reports an 11% rise in net profits for the first half of the year on stronger sales margins. Net profits at the privately-held firm rose to $64.36 million in the six months to June 30 from $57.78 million in the same period a year earlier. Puma has expanded rapidly through acquisitions in Australia last year and Papua New Guinea this year, but the company says focus in the second half will be on integrating existing acquisitions. (sarah.kent@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:04 EDT - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  devoted a large portion of her Jackson Hole speech last Friday to discuss the sluggish wage growth of recent years. More grist for that debate came this morning from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Labor Department\f28 \uc2 \f2 's biennial displaced workers survey. In the 2010 and 2012 surveys, which tracked job losses during and after the recession, a majority of workers who had lost full-time jobs they had held for at least three years, then found new full-time jobs, were making less money. In this year's survey, a slim majority--52%--were making the same or more. That's not back to pre-recession levels, but it's an improvement. (ben.leubsdorf@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11:04 EDT - The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Richmond Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's August manufacturing survey pointed to firmer business conditions. However, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes that hasn't been the trend thus far with other regional surveys this month. "Richmond is the 4th manufacturing survey we have received for August and so far was the only one to improve; Empire, Philly and Dallas all fell on an ISM-adjusted basis." (pedro.dacosta@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1503 GMT Hungary will reduce its public debt to around 80% of GDP or even below that by year-end from the current 85.1%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. Citi economist Eszter Gargyan explains that the government may also make use of its fiscal cash reserves to push the debt level below the end-2013 mark of 79.3% of GDP. Given that foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denominated public debt will remain close to 30% of GDP by year-end, the EUR/HUF exchange rate should remain around current levels or HUF should strengthen to help the government reduce its debt. "Therefore, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to communicate a neutral or cautious stance and is unlikely to cut rates further this year," Ms. Gargyan says. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 26, 2014 11:51 ET (15:51 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140826ea8q002ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
