\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan edges up vs dollar as sentiment stays bullish\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2014\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose against the\par dollar again on Tuesday, as investors remained bullish on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and corporate dollar sales helped offset a weaker\par midpoint fix by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate at\par 6.1663 per dollar prior to market open, down 0.02 percent from\par the previous fix.\par     The relatively weak midpoint is in line with global\par resurgence of the dollar of late, traders said. The spot\par rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above or below the\par midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1540 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1520 by midday, up 0.05 percent from the\par previous close.\par     The yuan also rose on Monday. Sentiment towards it has\par strengthened since May, when China began posting strong trade\par surpluses that boost dollar supply in the market, traders said.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1663     6.1653    -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1520     6.1550    0.05%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.23%               \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.59%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.53%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 