\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan firms slightly after last week's fall\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2014\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed slightly\par against the dollar on Monday, with technical buying helping to\par offset a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  midpoint fixing after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's largest weekly loss in two months last week. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint at 6.1653 per\par dollar prior to market open, down 0.06 percent from the previous\par fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1550 per dollar, and was\par changing hands at 6.1516 by midday, 0.02 percent stronger from\par the previous close.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1653     6.1617    -0.06%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1516     6.1529    0.02%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.22%               \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.59%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.54%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1555   -0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2350   -1.12%\par  forwards               **               \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHI